msgid "Automatic blocking"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:478
msgid "Actually refuse an address once a sensor threshold is passed. Off, the sensors only record."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:486
msgid "Block duration (hours)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:487
msgid "How long a first block lasts before the address is allowed back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:495
msgid "Community block threshold (%)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:496
msgid "The community confidence value from which an address is refused. Lower catches more and produces more false positives; the floor is there because below it most of what is caught is ordinary visitors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:502
msgid "Escalation ladder"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:503
msgid "Make each repeat offence last longer than the one before it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:511
msgid "Escalation ladder steps (minutes)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:512
msgid "The rungs of the ladder in minutes, shortest first. An address that keeps coming back moves up one rung per offence."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:520
msgid "Ladder reset window (days)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:521
msgid "How long an address must behave before it drops back to the first rung."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:528
msgid "Record every decision without acting on any of it. Use this to see what the settings would do before letting them do it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:536
msgid "Refuse addresses on the signed Tor exit-node list. Anonymity is not an attack in itself, so this is off unless your site has a reason."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:542
msgid "Contact URL on the block page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:543
msgid "Where a wrongly blocked visitor can reach you. Without it the block page is a dead end for a customer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:550
msgid "Firewall enabled"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:551
msgid "Inspect every front-end request against attack signatures before it reaches your site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:557
msgid "Firewall report-only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-registry.php:558
